## How Search Works in Newbury

Newbury's position on a main road crossroads shapes who searches for its businesses. Newbury is the main town in West Berkshire. West Berkshire Council has its offices on Market Street. The A34 runs past the town north to south. Junction 13 of the M4 at Chieveley is just to the north.

Most Newbury firms deal with three kinds of searcher.

**Residents** look for trades, clinics, solicitors, accountants and shops near home. Google's map results handle most of these searches. Your Google Business Profile, your reviews and a service page that names Newbury do most of the work.

**Businesses buying from businesses** judge suppliers on detailed service pages and evidence. A map listing is not enough for them. Vodafone has its head office at Vodafone House on The Connection in Newbury. Greenham Business Park is home to more than 150 businesses.

**Visitors** come for Newbury Racecourse and the Kennet and Avon Canal through the town centre. Pubs, restaurants, hotels and venues need to show up in the searches people make before they travel and on the day.

## West Berkshire in Numbers

West Berkshire is a district of small businesses: almost nine in ten have fewer than 10 staff.

| West Berkshire | Figure | Source |
|---|---:|---|
| VAT or PAYE registered businesses, 2026 | 8,140 | ONS UK Business Counts |
| Share with fewer than 10 staff | 88.4% | ONS UK Business Counts |
| Population, 2021 Census | 161,400 | ONS Census 2021 |
| Population change, 2011 to 2021 | +4.9% | ONS Census 2021 |

The figures cover the whole of West Berkshire with Thatcham and Hungerford included. ONS does not publish them for Newbury town alone. The business counts are VAT or PAYE registered enterprises as of March 2026 ([ONS UK Business Counts](https://www.nomisweb.co.uk/datasets/idbrent)). The population figures come from the 2021 Census. Full links are in the sources list at the end of this page.

