## Greenham Business Park and B2B Firms

Greenham Business Park suppliers usually win on detailed pages rather than on map results. The park sits on the former RAF Greenham Common site. The Greenham Common Trust took the land over from the Ministry of Defence in 1997. The park is now mostly industrial and mixed-use space.

Buyers here are procurement teams, engineers and operations managers. They search for a capability, a standard or a product. They often search from anywhere in the UK. A single "Services" page does not win those searches.

What usually works better:

- One page per capability with the specifications, sectors and standards a buyer checks
- Case studies and certifications on the page where buyers and Google can both see them
- A site structure that makes the link between your services clear
- Content that answers the questions buyers ask before they shortlist a supplier

I'll help you decide which searches are worth owning. I'll then build the pages that can earn them.

## SEO for Thatcham Businesses

Thatcham businesses compete with Newbury firms for the same map searches. Thatcham is a separate town about three miles east of Newbury along the A4. Customers travel between the two. Thatcham trades, childcare providers and clinics can win work from Newbury. A Thatcham business can also lose map searches to bigger Newbury competitors.

A Thatcham business usually needs:

- A Google Business Profile with the right service area and categories
- A page that names Thatcham and the nearby areas you cover
- Reviews from local customers that mention the job and the town
- Clear opening hours and prices or price ranges
- An easy way to get in touch from a phone

## SEO for Hungerford Businesses

Hungerford shops need to be found before the trip as well as on the High Street. Hungerford is the westernmost of the three towns. Junction 14 of the M4 serves it. Its High Street is known for antiques dealers and independent shops such as the Hungerford Arcade. The town hosts a weekly market on Wednesdays.

Antiques and specialist retail draw buyers from well beyond the town. A Hungerford shop usually needs:

- A complete Google Business Profile with accurate opening hours and current photos
- Category or product pages that match what a collector or buyer would type
- Technical foundations that let those pages rank across the UK if you sell online

## How Long SEO Takes in West Berkshire

SEO timelines in West Berkshire depend on your site and your competitors. I won't promise a timeline before I've looked at both. Fixes to your Google Business Profile and technical problems can show changes within a few months. Content-led growth for competitive B2B searches takes longer.

My guide on [how long SEO takes](/blog/how-long-does-seo-take/) explains what affects it.

